{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Suppiya","html":"<article id='thag1.32'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.32 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.32 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Catutthavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Four </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Suppiyattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Suppiya </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ajaraṁ jīramānena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ll swap old age for the unaging, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tappamānena nibbutiṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>burning for quenching—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nimiyaṁ paramaṁ santiṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the ultimate peace, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yogakkhemaṁ anuttaran”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the supreme sanctuary from the yoke. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Suppiyo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
